  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "CfBWvRnfFW5ERTaWmWqXBvia9p8=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T18:51:09.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "\"Document-native systems\" (BIM Services LLC, Mar 2026): digital tools designed to work **directly with unstructured construction documents** \u2014 specifications, contracts, submittals, compliance files \u2014 rather than only with structured data.\n\nIn practice:\n- Automatically extracting submittal requirements from specifications\n- Generating structured outputs (Excel/Word today)\n- Natural-language queries over project documents: *\"List all submittals under Division 07\"*\n- Turning hours of manual document review into minutes\n\nFraming on the human role: AI handles repetitive document review, information extraction, and data organization; engineers, BIM coordinators, and managers keep judgment, planning, and site execution \u2014 a productivity tool, not a replacement.\n\nThe concept is externally-validated demand for what Powerhouse document models already are, with one decisive difference: document-native *retrofits* (extract from static files, emit Excel) recover structure after the fact, while documents **born structured** as document models never lose it. The extraction approach is still relevant as the migration path \u2014 LLM-scanning legacy analog documents into structured models is exactly the on-ramp proposed in the DT BAU engagement (02:07:18).",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T18:51:09.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T18:51:09.000Z"
    }
  },
